        "trusted": false
      },
      {
        "caution_id": "evidence-gap:844fcda9d7b25549ba9a7449",
        "description": "Kernel-specific input conditions: Pseudotime, developmental potential, experimental time and metabolic labels are alternative views. Do not combine all inputs with ALL_OF or require RNA velocity for every CellRank analysis.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "content_hash": "5315ef10eca8f0e36b7b9fba52acbb66463d13bb2e1239fb3da099ff39158819",
            "end_offset": 62145,
            "evidence_span_id": "evidence-span:9425c7d5432c7276d6ccfffd",
            "exact_text": "A conceptual overview of kernels in CellRank 2. Decoupling infer-\nence of transition probability from their analysis. The typical CellRank \n2 workflow consists of two steps: (1) estimating cell–cell transition \nprobabilities and (2) deriving biological insights based on these esti-\nmates. Previously, we tied these two steps together14 but realized that \ndecoupling them yields a much more powerful and flexible modeling \nframework. Treating each step separately is possible as analyzing transi-\ntion matrices is independent of their construction. For example, esti-\nmating transition probabilities based on RNA velocity or a pseudotime \ndoes not change how initial and terminal states are inferred or fate prob-\nabilities estimated. Consequently, modularizing our problem-specific \nframework generalizes the corresponding analysis tools to other data \nmodalities. The two steps of our inference workflow are conceptualized \nby kernels and estimators, respectively.\nKernels estimate transition matrices T ∈ℝnc×nc at a cellular resolu-\ntion with nc denoting the number of cells; row Tj,: represents the transition \nprobabilities of cell j toward putative descendants. With CellRank 2, \nwe provide means to quantify fate probabilities based on RNA velocity \n(VelocityKernel), pseudotime (PseudotimeKernel), a developmental \npotential (CytoTRACEKernel), experimental time points (RealTimeK-\nernel) and metabolic labeling (metabolic-labeling-based vector field \nwith the VelocityKernel).",
            "locator": {
              "kind": "pdf_page",
              "value": "source-artifact:bdddbe8c5972df154c3c6bb79a1e2822/text-sha256:da8d619bee33cb0605615e1128bdeed2caa31467779137b8e6c04474e9ef1e2e:60661:62145"
            },
            "ontology_version": "2.0.0-core-review.1",
            "page": 11,
            "schema_version": "sckg-ontology-core-5c-design-v1",
            "source_artifact_id": "source-artifact:bdddbe8c5972df154c3c6bb79a1e2822",
            "source_revision_id": "source-revision:b80c4ef1dd9f3b9417e2e5c1",
            "start_offset": 60661
          }
        ],
        "execution_authorized": false,
        "execution_gate": false,
        "human_review_status": "pending",
        "production_retrieval_eligible": false,
